-- title:
--   Raising the order of an Euler–Maclaurin tail
-- statement:
--   Let $k\ge1$, $N\ge1$, and $s\in\mathbb C$ with $\operatorname{Re}s>0$. For
--   the defined coefficient $c_k$, tail $T_k=\operatorname{emTail}(s,N,k)$, and
--   Bernoulli number $B_{k+1}$,
--   $$T_k=\frac{B_{k+1}(-c_k(s)N^{-s-k})}{k+1}-\frac{T_{k+1}}{k+1}.$$
--   This is one integration-by-parts step on the infinite tail.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/DrMurphyIsIn/Arda/blob/af4fde8972eb6d4e78c7d9a95933b18b81adf52d/telperion/examples/zeta_reflection/lean/EMZetaHigh.lean#L131-L209

